@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-hourly-rental-rules
+type: decision-log
+title: "Hourly rental rules"
+status: pending
+---
+
+# Hourly rental rules
+
+## Context
+Visitors want a board for an afternoon; until now only whole days (dl-001) could be rented.
+
+## Decision
+- A rental is hourly when `end` - `start` is above 0 and under 24 hours and both are on the hour (UTC);
+  it may cross midnight. Anything else follows the whole-day rules of dl-001.
+- Total is `hours * hourlyPrice`; the long rental discount (dl-003) never applies, being below 3 days.
+- `hourlyPrice` is optional, a non-negative integer of cents. Without it, an hourly request throws.
+- A period under a day that is not on the hour (or mixes days and hours) is rejected, as before.
+- Bookings share the half-open overlap rule, so hourly and daily bookings of an item exclude each other.
+- `availability` is unchanged: it still queries whole days.
+
+## Consequences
+A 24-hour or longer rental must still be whole days. Hourly availability can be added later.
